From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:43:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: add google,zuma-pmu

zuma (Tensor G3) has gs101's PMU arrangement: PMU_ALIVE is writable only
from EL3. Add its compatible on its own: the register map differs from
gs101's, and it needs no pmu-intr-gen syscon for now (no CPU idle or
hotplug support yet).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
index 5bd39876e..14caf5bdc 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ properties:
     oneOf:
       - enum:
           - google,gs101-pmu
+          - google,zuma-pmu
       - items:
           - enum:
               - samsung,exynos3250-pmu
